from evaluate_models import *
import random,collections,platform

def paired(a,b):
 a={r['id']:r for r in a if r['positive']};b={r['id']:r for r in b if r['positive']};assert a.keys()==b.keys()
 gains=sum(not a[k]['top3'] and b[k]['top3'] for k in a);loss=sum(a[k]['top3'] and not b[k]['top3'] for k in a);n=gains+loss
 pv=min(1,2*sum(math.comb(n,j) for j in range(min(gains,loss)+1))/2**n) if n else 1
 groups=collections.defaultdict(list)
 for k in a:groups[a[k]['video_id']].append(int(b[k]['top3'])-int(a[k]['top3']))
 keys=sorted(groups);rng=random.Random(20261016);ds=[]
 for _ in range(2000):
  vals=[v for k in rng.choices(keys,k=len(keys)) for v in groups[k]];ds.append(sum(vals)/len(vals))
 return dict(n=len(a),gains=gains,losses=loss,delta=sum(int(b[k]['top3'])-int(a[k]['top3']) for k in a)/len(a),mcnemar_exact_two_sided_p=pv,paired_video_bootstrap95=np.percentile(ds,[2.5,97.5]).tolist(),replicates=2000,seed=20261016)
def pct(x):return f'{100*x:.2f}%'
def interval(v):return f'[{pct(v[0])}, {pct(v[1])}]'
def main():
 guard();d={f'{m}-{p}':load(R/f'{m}-{p}.json') for m in ['740m','270m'] for p in ['historical','android']};pa={p:paired(d['740m-'+p]['results']['test']['rows'],d['270m-'+p]['results']['test']['rows']) for p in ['historical','android']};save('paired-comparison.json',pa)
 a=d['740m-android'];b=d['270m-android'];ga=a['results']['test']['groups']['all'];gb=b['results']['test']['groups']['all'];p740=ga['metrics']['retrieval_top3_time_hit'];p270=gb['metrics']['retrieval_top3_time_hit'];ci=gb['top3_wilson95'];drop=p740-p270;rule1=drop<=.03;rule2=ci[0]<=p740<=ci[1];adopt=rule1 or rule2
 decision=dict(decision='ADOPT' if adopt else 'NOT ADOPT',hit3_drop_pp=100*drop,rule_drop_le_3pp=rule1,rule_740m_inside_270m_wilson95=rule2,baseline_point=p740,candidate_point=p270,candidate_wilson95=ci,threshold=b['threshold']);save('decision.json',decision)
 lines=['# EmbeddingGemma 2 text-270M evaluation','',f'**Decision: {decision["decision"]} 270M; build 1.0.4 (versionCode 5), local only.** Hit@3 drop = {100*drop:.2f} percentage points (≤3 pp: {rule1}); current Android-prefix LiteRT 740M point {pct(p740)} lies within 270M Wilson 95% CI {interval(ci)}: {rule2}. Both user rules pass. These rules do not establish statistical equivalence or broad generalization.','', 'AI-audited gold, not human listening ground truth. No gold/queries/transcripts/segments/splits were edited or filtered. All 31 low-confidence gold labels remain.','', '## Protocol and historical reproduction','', 'Primary comparison: exact frozen iter5 full corpus (1161 SenseVoice windows from all 14 videos), 140 AI-audited queries, real-dev 40 / real-test 100; test positives 62, negatives 38. Same frozen `eval_real.evaluate`, video+window-midpoint within gold answer interval; cosine full 768-D, stable score sort, Top-10 retained, Top-3 no deduplication/no refusal. No translation or candidate-video restriction. Threshold only annotates low confidence; Top-3 remains visible. Query origin video defines clustering. No test-based parameter tuning.','', 'Task requirements contain two different prefix protocols. Historical iter1/iter5: query `task: search result | query: ` and empty document prefix. Current Android AppConfig: query `task: search query | text: ` and document `task: search result | text: `. We ran both separately and use Android prefixes for the adoption/release threshold. A frozen desktop score must not be described as a device measurement.','', 'The original historical 740M is HF BF16 text-tower inference (CPU2, batch8), not `.litertlm`. Replaying the archived rankings through the frozen evaluator exactly reproduces Hit@1=36/62 and Hit@3=47/62. Fresh HF queries against the archived HF corpus also reproduce those exact hit decisions. Fresh HF corpus + fresh queries yields Hit@1=35/62, Hit@3=47/62; the maximum vector difference and bridge evidence are in `eval-270m/historical-reproduction.json`. Our transformers is 5.20.2 vs archived lock 5.19.0; NumPy 2.5.4 vs 2.5.2; Torch 2.14.1+cpu and sentence-transformers 6.1.0 match. Fresh batch numeric differences can affect close ranks. No historical file or one-shot marker was touched.','', 'LiteRT-LM Python 0.18.1, CPU4 single requests, normalizes output, explicit output_size=768, default special-token/overflow behavior. Android uses Kotlin 0.18.0. 740M loads its CPU vision/audio backends as in Android; 270M initializes only the text backend. No image/audio inference. Historical-prefix LiteRT 740M yields 36/62 Top-1 and 46/62 Top-3: net one fewer Top-3 than original HF (runtime/export numeric differences; two losses and one gain). Thus exact historical inference reproduction is **not** claimed; the scoring/data replay passes, and the controlled LiteRT pair is valid for the intended packaged model swap. Both LiteRT files run, so an HF-only model substitution was unnecessary.','', 'Wilson intervals below use positive queries as trials (requested supplementary statistic). Queries within a video are correlated; the historical iter5 interval was video-cluster bootstrap, not Wilson. Both are retained in JSON; paired delta uses video-cluster bootstrap (2000 draws, seed 20261016), with exact McNemar diagnostic. Historical iter1 event-level Wilson is not interchangeable with these query-level intervals.','', '## Side-by-side real-test results','', '| Prefix protocol / model | Hit@1 | Wilson 95% | Hit@3 | Wilson 95% | Top-1 timestamp median / p90 (s) |', '| --- | ---: | --- | ---: | --- | --- |']
 for p in ['historical','android']:
  for m in ['740m','270m']:
   g=d[m+'-'+p]['results']['test']['groups']['all'];me=g['metrics'];err=g['top1_timestamp_error_s_same_video_only'];lines.append(f'| {p} / {m} | {round(me["retrieval_top1_time_hit"]*62)}/62 ({pct(me["retrieval_top1_time_hit"])}) | {interval(g["top1_wilson95"])} | {round(me["retrieval_top3_time_hit"]*62)}/62 ({pct(me["retrieval_top3_time_hit"])}) | {interval(g["top3_wilson95"])} | {err["median"]:.3f} / {err["p90"]:.3f} (n={err["n"]}) |')
 lines+=['','Timestamp error is absolute Top-1 midpoint distance to nearest gold answer center, **conditional on correct video**, over positive queries. Wrong-video predictions have undefined time distance and are excluded; n is explicit. Hit metrics still count those as misses. This is a new descriptive extension, not a replacement for frozen interval-hit scoring.','', '| Paired Top-3 comparison | Gains / losses | Δ270M−740M | Paired video bootstrap 95% | McNemar exact p |','| --- | ---: | ---: | --- | ---: |']
 for p,x in pa.items():lines.append(f'| {p} | {x["gains"]} / {x["losses"]} | {100*x["delta"]:.2f} pp | {interval(x["paired_video_bootstrap95"])} | {x["mcnemar_exact_two_sided_p"]:.4f} |')
 lines+=['','## Android-prefix language breakdown (real-test positives)','', '| Group | 740M Hit@1 / Hit@3 | 270M Hit@1 / Hit@3 | 270M Hit@3 Wilson 95% |','| --- | --- | --- | --- |']
 for name in ['zh','en','cross_language']:
  x=a['results']['test']['groups'][name];y=b['results']['test']['groups'][name];n=y['metrics']['positive_n'];lines.append(f'| {name}, n={n} | {pct(x["metrics"]["retrieval_top1_time_hit"])} / {pct(x["metrics"]["retrieval_top3_time_hit"])} | {pct(y["metrics"]["retrieval_top1_time_hit"])} / {pct(y["metrics"]["retrieval_top3_time_hit"])} | {interval(y["top3_wilson95"])} |')
 lines+=['','Cross-language overlaps zh/en. No positive-query category strata exist in this protocol; negative types affect no-answer diagnostics rather than positive Hit@3. Both dev/test full per-query rankings and all original group metrics/bootstrap intervals are retained.','', '## Confidence calibration','', 'Reused exactly the iter1 S2 method and its 76-query calibration split (52 positive / 24 negative), frozen calibration windows/targets: choose the lowest score boundary with negative accepted fraction ≤0.10, accepting score≥threshold; include float64 `nextafter(+∞)` boundaries. This is not F1 optimization for wrong-Top-1 detection. No real-test score entered threshold selection.','', f'New Android-prefix 270M threshold: **{b["threshold"]!r}**. Both paired models select the same value. Historical-prefix 270M threshold: **{d["270m-historical"]["threshold"]!r}**. Do not reuse the old HF historical-prefix 0.7889297604560853 after a runtime/prefix change. All candidate boundaries/FPR counts are saved in `*-threshold-curve.json`; chosen boundary and raw rankings were saved before test ranking.','', '| Split (270M Android prefixes) | Wrong Top-1 | Flagged | Correctly flagged | Precision | Recall |','| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |']
 c=load(R/'270m-android-threshold.json');stats=[('iter1 calibration',c['flagging'])]+[(s,b['results'][s]['wrong_top1_flagging']) for s in ['dev','test']]
 for name,x in stats:lines.append(f'| {name} (n={x["n"]}) | {x["wrong_top1_n"]} | {x["flagged_n"]} | {x["true_positive_n"]} | {pct(x["precision"])} | {pct(x["recall"])} |')
 lines+=['',f'Calibration negatives accepted: {c["negative_false_accept_n"]}/{c["negative_n"]} = 8.33%. Wrong Top-1 means no target (including all negative queries) or Top-1 outside the gold localization rule. Iter1 uses same-video midpoint error ≤2s; iter5 uses its gold tolerance interval. Flag means score<threshold. The empirical false-accept cap is calibration-only, not a correctness probability or guaranteed test risk.','', '## Box embedding cost','', '| Android prefixes | Load (s) | Corpus request median / p90 (ms) | Query request median / p90 (ms) | Peak process RSS (MiB) |','| --- | ---: | --- | --- | ---: |']
 for m in ['740m','270m']:
  x=d[m+'-android'];parts=[]
  for k in ['corpus','query']:
   vals=[v['seconds']*1000 for v in x['timing'] if v['kind']==k];parts.append(f'{np.median(vals):.2f} / {np.percentile(vals,90):.2f}')
  lines.append(f'| {m} | {x["load_seconds"]:.3f} | {parts[0]} | {parts[1]} | {x["peak_rss_mib"]:.2f} |')
 lines+=['', 'Shared x86_64 CPU box, four runtime threads; warm filesystem/cache, no affinity or idle guarantee, one run per model/protocol, other setup/HF/ASR jobs may overlap. ru_maxrss is whole-process high-water RSS, including imports/backends. These are descriptive box costs, not randomized benchmarks, device latency, or device RAM. Individual request timings are preserved in JSON.','', '## Official smaller SenseVoice packages','', '| Official package | Archive bytes | ONNX bytes | ONNX SHA-256 |','| --- | ---: | ---: | --- |']
 packs=load(R/'asr-packages.json')
 for x in packs:lines.append(f'| int8 {x["date"]} | {x["archive_bytes"]:,} | {x["files"]["model.int8.onnx"]["bytes"]:,} | `{x["files"]["model.int8.onnx"]["sha256"]}` |')
 lines+=['', 'The 2024 int8-only ONNX **and tokens are byte-identical** to current packaged files, so there is no installed-footprint saving; only archive packaging shrinks versus the mixed 1,047,870,769-byte archive. The 2025 file saves 2,118,294 bytes (~0.89%). Both official download URLs and archive/file hashes are retained; release URLs are tag-addressed rather than immutable, so SHA-256 identifies the actual bytes.','']
 if (R/'asr-results.json').exists():
  ar=load(R/'asr-results.json');lines+=['| Paired ONNX pipeline | Windows | Test Hit@1 | Test Hit@3 | Whisper disagreement proxy CER |','| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |']
  for name,x in ar.items():lines.append(f'| {name} | {x["corpus_windows"]} | {pct(x["test"]["metrics"]["retrieval_top1_time_hit"])} | {pct(x["test"]["metrics"]["retrieval_top3_time_hit"])} | {pct(x["whisper_proxy_cer"]["rate"])} |')
  if len(ar)==2:
   older=ar['2024-07-17'];new=ar['2025-09-09'];delta=new['test']['metrics']['retrieval_top3_time_hit']-older['test']['metrics']['retrieval_top3_time_hit'];lines+=['',f'2025−2024 downstream Hit@3 change: {100*delta:.2f} pp. Keep the existing 2024 ONNX in 1.0.4: the small byte saving does not justify a pipeline/model change with any regression or mixed metric evidence. The int8-only 2024 download is interchangeable but does not change installed bytes.']
 lines+=['', 'ASR comparison: all original 14 raw 16k mono WAVs; identical Silero `faster_whisper.vad` max6s/min_silence300ms spans shared between variants; sherpa-onnx 1.13.8 CPU2, greedy, language auto, ITN on. Same 740M LiteRT Android-prefix embedder for both, same frozen gold/splits/midpoint hit evaluator. Tokens/timestamps are sherpa BPE tokens; token end is next token timestamp (final token capped at +60ms and VAD end), then unchanged iter1 `transcript_windows` grouping. The historical corpus used FunASR FP32 word timestamps: its 1161 windows cannot remain fixed when measuring a different ASR. These paired ONNX results are a separate ASR diagnostic, not an embedding A/B replacement for the frozen corpus. Android VAD itself uses max4s/min_silence250ms, unlike this real-test pipeline; device regression remains untested.','', 'No human reference transcript exists. “CER” here is only normalized full-video ASR disagreement against the same frozen independent Whisper transcript (NFKC/lowercase/alphanumeric chars); it is **not** true human CER or proof of recognition accuracy. Keep that limitation with the number.','', '## Provenance, reproducibility and scope','', f'270M repo: [pinned model card](https://huggingface.co/litert-community/embeddinggemma-2-text-270m-litert-lm/tree/9be6e8b90982095dc05c2bd162e4b954ee4dbac7), file `embeddinggemma-2-text-270m.litertlm`, 164,626,432 bytes, SHA-256 `{b["model_sha256"]}`. 740M SHA-256 `{a["model_sha256"]}` (484,622,336 bytes), pinned revision `24d962e906c7d332c6428e71c9676855024569e2`. 270M native output verified at 768 dimensions; FULL_DIM/DB vector shape stays 768, but generation must change to prevent mixed-model indices. Text-only packaged model removes 319,995,904 bytes.','', 'Runtime reference: [LiteRT-LM embedding API](https://ai.google.dev/edge/litert-lm/embedding_models); [official SenseVoice packages](https://k2-fsa.github.io/sherpa/onnx/sense-voice/pretrained.html). Inference is entirely local. HTTP downloads only fetched public runtime/model inputs; no remote Git contact, push, media upload or store action. Secrets were neither read nor printed.','', 'Evidence and scripts: `eval-270m/input-manifest.json`, `historical-reproduction.json`, `{740m,270m}-{historical,android}.json`, `*-threshold.json`, `paired-comparison.json`, `decision.json`, `asr-packages.json`, `asr-results.json`, per-video ASR JSON and VAD spans; logs `logs/eval-270m-*.log`. Scripts write only evaluation outputs; they import the frozen evaluator rather than its one-shot CLI. Archived frozen markers are never reset. This authorized new-model comparison is a new retrospective experiment, not the original one-shot test or unseen heldout validation.','', 'Reproduce with the recorded `requirements.txt`, cached pinned model files, then `python evaluate_models.py --model {740m,270m} --protocol {historical,android}` (one combination per invocation), `python reproduce_historical.py`, `python evaluate_asr.py`, `python report_evaluation.py`; retain completed outputs in a separate copied output directory for a new run. Delete only generated runtime/build intermediates. Original frozen files remain read-only; input hashes are rechecked at completion.','', 'Release artifacts, checks, storage estimates, screenshots, source mirror and local commit: [REPORT-1.0.4.md](REPORT-1.0.4.md). Physical-device acceptance remains pending.']
 lines+=['', (R/'grok-audit-section.md').read_text().rstrip()]
 (B/'release/EVAL-270M.md').write_text('\n'.join(lines)+'\n');print(json.dumps(decision))
